      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I meant is that in the case of propagating the boolean constant, most cases are true for `variable-\u003eGetUses().HasExactlyOneElement()`. Haven\u0027t tested the other one.\n\nOne of the reasons for this is that before GVN the comparisons are not going to have deduplication. I tested a prototype of \"Aggressive\" constant folding that would only call into `PropagateValue` for booleans after GVN happened but didn\u0027t see that much improvement. Probably because we just do `variable-\u003eGetUses().HasExactlyOneElement()` and return.\n\n\u003e If yes, then we should probably do this check before loading the stats_ for the recording_stats check. (Additional optimization opportunity for this or another CL.)\n\nDoing that SGTM. Shouldn\u0027t see that much improvement in the common case (the one where stats_ is not null) but it doesn\u0027t hurt to add regardless. Will do in a follow-up",
